  "writeup": {
    "approach": "The communal heart of the house is a rear living and dining room lit by a large flush rooflight, with French doors to the outside. The finish is pitched well above the standard letting specification: wall lights either side of a sculptural panel, cane and black timber dining chairs, and a soft palette that reads as a home rather than a room let by the week.",
    "outcome": "Complete and let. HMO Designers worked as part of the wider project team on this scheme rather than as sole designer, so the credit is shared with the others involved."
  },
  "projectStory": {
    "summary": [
      "An ultra-luxury eight-bedroom HMO in Portsmouth, created from an existing dwelling as high-specification accommodation for professional tenants.",
      "The heart of the house is the rear living and dining space, lit by a large flush rooflight with French doors opening outside. Wall lights either side of a sculptural panel, cane and black timber dining chairs and a soft palette make the room read as a home rather than a room let by the week.",
      "HMO Designers, part of Thistle Group, worked as part of a collaborative design and build team on this project rather than as the sole designer.",
      "The scheme is complete and let, and is a good example of the standard of accommodation now coming to the top end of the HMO market."
